@startuml
title I2CIP - Module Orchestration and Runtime

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty members

package "I2CIP Namespace" {
  object RuntimeAPI {
    +commandRouter(command: JsonObject, out: Print): void
    +rebuildTree(out: Print, update: bool=false): void
    --
    {static} devicetree: BST<i2cip_fqa_t, Device*>
    {static} modules: Module*[8]
    {static} errlev: i2cip_errorlevel_t[8]
  }
}

package "Topology and Grouping" {
  class DeviceGroup {
    -key: i2cip_id_t
    -numdevices: uint8_t
    -devices: Device*[8]
    +factory: factory_device_t
    +handler: jsonhandler_device_t
    +cleanup: cleanup_device_t
    --
    +create<C>(id: i2cip_id_t): DeviceGroup*
    +operator[](fqa: i2cip_fqa_t): Device*
    +operator()(fqa: i2cip_fqa_t): Device*
  }

  class Module {
    -wire: uint8_t
    -mux: uint8_t
    -devicegroups: HashTable<DeviceGroup>
    -eeprom_added: bool
    #eeprom: EEPROM*
    --
    +operator[](id: i2cip_id_t): DeviceGroup*
    +operator()(): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +discoverEEPROM(recurse: bool=false): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +parseEEPROMContents(contents: const char*): bool
    +toJSON(obj: JsonObject, pingFilter: bool=false): void
    +handleCommand(command: JsonObject, out: Print): void
    +handleConfig(config: JsonObject, out: Print): void
    +handleInterval(intervals: JsonObject, out: Print): void
    +handleEvent(event: JsonObject, out: Print): void
  }

  class JsonModule
  class NotAModule
}

' Cross-diagram references (see uml-device.puml and uml-containers.puml)
package "Core Device Model" {
  class Device
  class EEPROM
}
package "Topology and Grouping" {
  class "BST<K,T>" as BST
  class "HashTable<T>" as HashTable
}

JsonModule --|> Module
NotAModule --|> Module

RuntimeAPI o-- BST : devicetree
RuntimeAPI o-- Module : modules[0..7]
Module *-- EEPROM
Module *-- HashTable : DeviceGroup table
DeviceGroup o-- Device : devices[0..7]

Module ..> Device : add/remove/operate
Module ..> DeviceGroup : find/create
RuntimeAPI ..> Module : command routing
RuntimeAPI ..> JsonModule : EEPROM JSON parsing implementation

note right of RuntimeAPI
Global orchestration state is owned
by namespace-level variables:
- devicetree
- modules[]
- errlev[]
end note

note bottom of Module
Module is the subnet orchestrator for one wire+MUX pair.

Core duties:
- validate subnet ownership for FQAs
- discover and parse EEPROM configuration
- manage DeviceGroups (ID -> factory + instances)
- execute command/config/event handlers
- serialize module state as JSON

The module always owns exactly one EEPROM endpoint.
end note

note right of DeviceGroup
DeviceGroup binds an ID string to:
- a device factory
- JSON argument parser/cleanup hooks
- up to I2CIP_DEVICES_PER_GROUP concrete instances

operator()(fqa):
lookup existing instance OR create via factory.
end note

note left of JsonModule
JsonModule provides the reference implementation of
parseEEPROMContents() that deserializes EEPROM payload,
resolves DeviceGroups by ID, and materializes devices
into the global tree/module structures.
end note

note left of NotAModule
NotAModule is a compatibility façade for devices not
physically behind a real hardware module.

It preserves Module-based call patterns while using
fake MUX/bus addressing conventions.
end note

note as N_flow
Typical runtime flow (command by FQA):
1) RuntimeAPI::commandRouter()
2) Route to modules[m]
3) Module resolves/creates Device via DeviceGroup/BST
4) Device performs MUX setBus + transport operation
5) Interface layer updates typed cache/value state
6) Optional MUX reset and module error aggregation
end note

RuntimeAPI .. N_flow

@enduml
